# 9. BUILDING SYSTEM

Every building must have:

- A unique ID.
- A building type.
- An owner player ID.
- An X coordinate.
- A Y coordinate.
- Health.
- Building-specific variables.

## 9.1 Mine

Cost: 1 point.

Health: 1.

Properties:

- Only visible to the player who placed it.
- Does not block movement.
- When another player moves onto it, that player loses 1 health.
- Mines can be destroyed by attacks.
- When removed during round progression, they must play an explosion animation.

The mine's lifecycle after triggering must be documented explicitly because the original design does not specify whether it is consumed immediately.

## 9.2 Outpost

Cost: 1 point.

Health: 2.

Purpose:

- Blocks player movement.

It must be possible to destroy an outpost by attacking it.

It must be removed when health reaches 0.

## 9.3 Nuclear silo

Cost: 2 points.

Health: 1.

Properties:

- Starts empty.
- Starts inactive.
- Automatically becomes armed on the following day.
- Its owner can use it once armed.
- Can target any coordinate because it has unlimited range.
- Damages a 3 × 3 area around the chosen coordinate.

Damage:

- Center square: 2 damage.
- All eight surrounding squares: 1 damage.

A launch must have a travel animation and explosion animation.

The silo can be attacked and destroyed like other buildings.

The launch cost, number of launches, and any cooldown must be explicitly resolved before finalizing the mechanic. Do not silently assume these rules.

## 9.4 Bank

Cost: 1 point.

Health: 1.

Initial value: 1.

Properties:

- Value increases by 1 each day.
- Maximum value: 5.
- Can be claimed by its owner.
- Claiming costs 1 point.
- Claiming gives the player points equal to the bank's current value.
- Claiming is considered a building action, therefore it has priority 3.
- It can be destroyed by attacks.

The exact timing of value increases and what happens to a bank after it is claimed must be documented explicitly.

