# 11. ANIMATION AND VISUAL FEEDBACK

All game actions must produce visual playback when a player progresses to the next day.

Animations must follow the actual server-calculated execution order.

Required visual effects:

MOVEMENT:

- Tween the player's position to the destination square.

BUILDING:

- Tween the building into existence through transparency.

HEALING:

- Show healing particles.

POINT TRANSFER:

- Display a yellow arrow from the sender to the recipient.
- Outline the receiving player.

ATTACK:

- Display a red arrow from the attacker to the attacked square.
- Outline the attacked square.

DAMAGED PLAYER:

- Show blood particles.

DESTROYED BUILDING:

- Tween its transparency until it disappears.

MINE ACTIVATION:

- Play an explosion animation when a player triggers a mine.

MINE DESTRUCTION:

- Play an explosion animation when a mine is removed.

NUCLEAR ATTACK:

- Animate the launched nuke travelling to its target.
- Play an explosion animation.
- Show the damage across the affected 3 × 3 area.

All effects must play during the "Progress to Next Day" experience.

Do not calculate damage or decide who died in the frontend.

The backend must provide an ordered list of events describing what actually happened.

The frontend must play those events.

Animations must never change authoritative health, points, building positions, or player positions.

