# 14. GAME END CONDITIONS

There are two main game-ending conditions.

## 14.1 World peace

Each player has a world peace vote.

During the open phase, players can change their vote.

If all required player votes are currently "yes", the game ends.

Statistics:

- Every player receives +1 games played.
- Every living player receives +1 world peaces.
- Each dead player receives +1 death when they die.

Determine and document how votes from dead players are handled.

## 14.2 Last player standing

If everyone dies except one player, the game ends.

Statistics:

- Every player receives +1 games played.
- The surviving player receives +1 last one standings.
- Each dead player receives +1 death when they die.

Do not award the last-one-standing statistic when the game ends through world peace.

## 14.3 No active game

When there is no active game:

- The game remains closed.
- Players cannot submit actions.
- The website displays the closed-game timer/state.
- An administrator can schedule a date to start a new game.

Do not automatically start another game.

Any new game has a new UUID, players can load a previously finished game and make it automatically play all days from 1 to the final one. Creating a timeline animation. (an already finished game shows mines transparently, doesnt hide them)

