# 16. ADMIN PANEL AND PLAYER MANAGEMENT

An administrator-only panel must be available.

The backend must check the authenticated player's admin status on every protected API operation.

Never rely only on hiding admin buttons in the frontend.

Administrators can:

- Create players.
- Generate invitation links.
- Reset a player's existing sessions.
- Generate new player sessions.
- Edit player usernames.
- Edit player profile picture URLs.

Creating a player must generate a link that can be shared with that player.

The link must let the player authenticate and receive a session cookie valid for 3 months.

Use a secure one-time invitation token that is exchanged for an authentication cookie rather than exposing a reusable session secret in the URL.

Session cookies must use appropriate security settings, including HttpOnly, Secure in production, and an appropriate SameSite policy.

Administrators must be able to revoke compromised sessions.

Only administrators can access player-management operations.

There must be a secure initial administrator bootstrap method that does not create a public admin-registration endpoint. Probably through environment variables.

